---
import Figure from "../Figure.astro";
// Four ways to climb the same toy landscape, one trial each, animated by src/figures/climb.ts.
---
<Figure width="wide">
  <div class="climb" id="climb"></div>
  <div class="racebar">
    <button class="playb" id="climbPlay" type="button">Pause</button>
    <input class="rng" type="range" id="climbT" min="0" max="200" step="1" value="0" aria-label="Evaluation" />
    <span class="num" id="climbTv"></span>
  </div>
  <div class="legend">
    <span><i style="background:var(--fig-ink)"></i>start</span>
    <span><i class="ln" style="background:#8A8A90"></i>a baseline's steps</span>
    <span><i class="ln" style="background:var(--fig-accent)"></i>SCiEL's steps</span>
    <span><i class="ln" style="background:var(--fig-chord)"></i>culture: a lagging line moves to the leader's finding</span>
    <span><i class="dash" style="border-top-color:var(--fig-accent)"></i>research probe</span>
  </div>
  <Fragment slot="caption">
    <b>Figure 3.</b> One trial each, 200 evaluations: one model sampled independently, one climber, five climbers
    that share nothing, and SCiEL. Contour lines show the score; hatching marks invalid solutions. Only SCiEL gets up the narrow ridge.
  </Fragment>
</Figure>
